title: Synthetic Monitoring: Journey
agents: linux
catalog: app/synmon
license: MIT
distribution: check_mk
description:
 One service per synthetic-monitoring journey, sourced from the worker's
 spool via the {synmon_journey} agent section (piggybacked to the logical
 target host). The service maps the executor's own status (0/1/2/3) and
 escalates on configurable total/per-step duration thresholds. A journey
 that succeeded only after retries is WARN by default (configurable). A
 stale result ({now} - {started_at} > {max_age_s} + grace) replaces the
 state with UNKNOWN by default (configurable), so availability/SLA reports
 can tell "no measurement" apart from an application outage. Per-step timings,
 the error, and artifact paths (screenshot/trace, stored on the worker) are
 shown in the service details. Perfdata: total duration, result age, and
 per-step durations.

 The service also reports Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP) plus FCP and
 TTFB as perfdata when the executor captures them. Configurable warn/crit
 thresholds for LCP, CLS, and INP are available in the ruleset.

 Configure thresholds and staleness handling with the ruleset
 "Synthetic monitoring: journey".
